### Tested versions

- Reproducible in: 4.7.2.stable.official (Windows, console build, headless)
- The same code is unchanged on `master` (checked `modules/gdscript/gdscript_vm.cpp` today); not run on master.

### System information

Windows 11 Pro 10.0.26200 - Godot v4.7.2.stable.official - headless - AMD Ryzen 9 3900X (12 cores)

### Issue description

Calling the same GDScript function for the first time from several threads at once can crash the engine with an access violation (`0xC0000005`), with no crash text printed (the crash happens on a worker thread).

The cause appears to be the first-run cache in `OPCODE_OPERATOR` (`modules/gdscript/gdscript_vm.cpp`). An operator on untyped operands is compiled with signature 0. On the first execution, the thread takes `initializer_mutex` and writes the cache:

```cpp
if (_code_ptr[ip + 5] == 0) {
    _code_ptr[ip + 5] = actual_signature;
    _code_ptr[ip + 6] = static_cast<int>(ret_type);
    Variant::ValidatedOperatorEvaluator *tmp = reinterpret_cast<Variant::ValidatedOperatorEvaluator *>(&_code_ptr[ip + 7]);
    *tmp = op_func;
}
```

But the fast path is read without the mutex:

```cpp
} else if (likely(op_signature == actual_signature)) {
    Variant::Type ret_type = static_cast<Variant::Type>(_code_ptr[ip + 6]);
    Variant::ValidatedOperatorEvaluator op_func = *reinterpret_cast<Variant::ValidatedOperatorEvaluator *>(&_code_ptr[ip + 7]);
    ...
    op_func(a, b, dst);
```

The signature at `ip + 5` is published before the return type and the evaluator pointer at `ip + 6` / `ip + 7`, with no ordering between them. A second thread executing the same site can read the new signature, take the optimized path, and call the pointer at `ip + 7` before it is written.

What we measured with the script below (8 threads, a function with 400 `x = x + b` sites, a fresh script each iteration):

| mode | result |
|---|---|
| `untyped`, called cold on the threads | crashed 4 runs of 4 (`0xC0000005`), within ~50-800 iterations |
| `typed` (`int` operands, compiled to `OPCODE_OPERATOR_VALIDATED`, no first-run cache) | 12,000 of 12,000 iterations ok |
| `warm`: untyped, but one call on the main thread first | 12,000 of 12,000 iterations ok |

Workaround: call the function once on one thread before handing it to worker threads, or type the operands.

A possible fix: write the signature last (after `ip + 6` and `ip + 7`) with release ordering and read it with acquire ordering, or keep the fast-path check behind the same publication order.

### Steps to reproduce

1. Save the script below as `op_race.gd` in an empty project.
2. Run: `godot --headless --path <project> --script res://op_race.gd -- mode=untyped iters=1000 threads=8 sites=400`
3. The process exits with an access violation (no crash text). Compare with `mode=typed` or `mode=warm`, which finish with `wrong=0`.

```gdscript
extends SceneTree
# mode=untyped|typed|warm iters=<K> threads=<T> sites=<N>

var _g: GDScript = null
var _sum: Array = []

func _initialize() -> void:
	var a: Dictionary = {}
	for s in OS.get_cmdline_user_args():
		var kv: PackedStringArray = s.split("=", true, 1)
		if kv.size() == 2:
			a[kv[0]] = kv[1]
	var mode: String = String(a.get("mode", "untyped"))
	var iters: int = int(a.get("iters", "200"))
	var threads: int = int(a.get("threads", "8"))
	var sites: int = int(a.get("sites", "400"))
	var body: String = ""
	if mode == "typed":
		body = "static func f(a: int, b: int) -> int:\n\tvar x: int = a\n"
	else:
		body = "static func f(a, b):\n\tvar x = a\n"
	for i in sites:
		body += "\tx = x + b\n"
	body += "\treturn x\n"
	var bad: int = 0
	for i in iters:
		_g = GDScript.new()
		_g.source_code = body
		if _g.reload() != OK:
			printerr("COMPILE FAILED")
			quit(2)
			return
		if mode == "warm":
			_g.call("f", 1, 2)
		_sum.resize(threads)
		_sum.fill(0)
		var gid: int = WorkerThreadPool.add_group_task(_one, threads, threads, true, "race")
		WorkerThreadPool.wait_for_group_task_completion(gid)
		for v in _sum:
			if int(v) != 1 + 2 * sites:
				bad += 1
	printerr("DONE mode=%s iters=%d threads=%d sites=%d wrong=%d" % [mode, iters, threads, sites, bad])
	quit(0 if bad == 0 else 1)

func _one(k: int) -> void:
	_sum[k] = _g.call("f", 1, 2)
```

### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)

The single script above is the whole reproduction (run with `--script`; no scene or project settings needed).
